ng service infrastructure"},{"capacity":"","location":"Bengaluru, Karnataka","role":"Engineering Development Centre (EDC) for indigenous product development"},{"capacity":"SMT capacity expanded to 32,000 PCBs per month","location":"Not specified (printer manufacturing)","role":"SMT line originally set up for set-top box production, later expanded for printer manufacturing"}],"pre":0,"products":"{\"Products & Solutions (PSG)\": [\"Dot matrix printers (DMP)\", \"Thermal printers\", \"Barcode scanners\", \"Keyboards\", \"Point-of-sale (POS) systems\", \"AIDC handheld devices and barcode solutions\", \"Offline UPS (Aegis, Elgar)\", \"'Made in India' integrated technology solutions\"], \"Customer Support Services (CSS)\": [\"L3/L4 repair and refurbishment services\", \"Field support and last-mile services\", \"Warranty, installation and break-fix support\", \"Infrastructure Management Services / remote IMS\", \"TVSE Aikya AI-driven Managed Services Platform (NOC, Automation, Cybersecurity)\"], \"Electronics …","promises":[],"promises_total":0,"promoters":[{"name":"Mr. Gopal Srinivasan (DIN: 00177699)","role":"Sole Promoter of the Company, directly holding 59.71% of the shareholding; also Chairman (Non-Executive, Non-Independent). Under the AOA he holds special rights so long as he holds not less than 26% of paid-up equity capital: the right to nominate up to two Directors on the Board and remove such nominees, to have a nominee Director considered for appointment as Managing Director (and remove them from that position), and to nominate one Director for appointment as Chairman (and remove such nominated Chairman). Shareholders approved by Postal Ballot on April 23, 2026 the amendment of the AOA to reflect him as the Promoter and the continuation/conferment of these special rights upon him."},{"name":"TVS Investments Private Limited (TVSI), formerly M/s. Sundaram Investment Limited","role":"Erstwhile Promoter identified under the earlier Articles of Association and original holder of the promoter special rights; pursuant to the Scheme it was amalgamated with the Company and ceased to exist without winding up, and consequently ceased to be a Promoter. There is no holding company for TVSE."}],"related":"[{\"name\": \"TVS Investments Private Limited (TVSI), formerly M/s. Sundaram Investment Limited\", \"relation\": \"related party\", \"note\": \"Erstwhile Promoter of the Company that was amalgamated with the Company pursuant to a Scheme and ceased to exist without winding up; the promoter special rights …","risks":[{"note":"The company swung from a pre-exceptional loss in the prior year to only a marginal profit before tax in 2025-26, and the turnaround rests on operational efficiencies, cost management, business mix and working capital optimisation rather than structural pricing power. Directors did not recommend any dividend for FY2026, citing current year performance and future growth needs.","risk":"Thin, volatile profitability with limited buffer"},{"note":"Revenue sits almost entirely in Products & Solutions (PSG) and Customer Support Services (CSS). PSG, the larger contributor, grew only ~3% versus 13% for CSS, so overall growth depends disproportionately on the services segment while the product business remains the bigger but slower base.","risk":"Concentration in two segments, with the larger one growing slowly"},{"note":"CSS growth is attributed to deeper engagement with key customers and the addition of new service engagements, and EMS scale-up depends on manufacturing orders secured from 'strategic customers'. Loss or non-renewal of a small number of anchor relationships would be material to both segments.","risk":"Dependence on a few key customers and service engagements"},{"note":"Electronic Manufacturing Services, Infrastructure Management Services and Green Energy are described as new growth areas being invested in, with EMS only 'laying a strong foundation for scaling up in the coming years'. Returns are back-ended and none of these has yet demonstrated scale or profitability.","risk":"Execution risk in unproven new growth verticals"},{"note":"The IMS/CSS business runs customer infrastructure across endpoints, data centres and cloud with a stated 99.99% availability commitment, NOC/SOC operations and 100% security patch compliance. The company itself flags 'evolving cybersecurity threats'; a breach or sustained availability failure at a client would carry direct contractual and reputational consequences.","risk":"Cybersecurity and service-availability exposure in managed services"},{"note":"With a 1000+ employee base and delivery through field engineers, service partners and engineering staff, the business model is labour-led. Management explicitly frames workforce attraction and retention (competitive compensation, career pathways, feedback mechanisms) as a critical enabler of sustained performance, making attrition a structural, not incidental, risk.","risk":"People-intensive model dependent on attracting and retaining talent"},{"note":"Strategy calls for investment in manufacturing infrastructure, assembly capabilities and PCB production to raise local value addition and compete for government and institutional opportunities. This shifts a historically asset-light distributor/service company toward fixed-cost manufacturing, raising operating leverage and utilisation risk.","risk":"Capital-intensive 'Make in India' manufacturing build-out"},{"note":"The cautionary statement expressly notes that actual outcomes on growth strategy, financial performance, product potential and development initiatives may differ materially from stated expectations, and that the company undertakes no obligation to update them.","risk":"Forward-looking growth plans subject to material variance"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"TVSELECT","sector":"Information Technology","sk":null,"strategies":"Strengthen Engineering and Product Development capabilities as a long-term growth platform|Expand the Electron